YARGRNP <YARGRNP@mailinator.temp.com> wrote:

> This is my first post to RGRN.  I'm one of those eternal nethack dabblers,  
> who's never persevered to ascension.

That, I think, is important.

> My question is: how does one maximize/optimize the desirable permanent  
> intrinsics one could potentially acquire?  I suppose this depends on  
> race/role and on the edibility of rings, etc, so what is the best  
> character to start with, and should I scum until I get a particular ring,  
> or anything?

You should never scum. It doesn't teach you to get by with what you
have. What you _should_ do is eat corpses as well as (or indeed, before)
rings.

> What would this list of intrinsics look like, and what would be missing  
> (or unavoidably based on luck, or tradeoffs with others)?  Fiddling a bit  
> in wizmode, I currently have:
> 
>    You are fire resistant.
>    You are cold resistant.
>    You are sleep resistant.
>    You are disintegration-resistant.
>    You are shock resistant.
>    You are poison resistant.
>    You see invisible.
>    You are telepathic.
>    You have automatic searching.
>    You have infravision.
>    You can survive without air.
>    You are fast.
> 
> What am I missing? (I can't have stealth or regeneration because those  
> rings happen to be inedible, and I don't consider permanent invisibility  
> "desirable".)

Reflection, magic resistance and at least MC2, but you can't get those
intrinsically. 
Teleport control. Polymorph control, if you wish - I rarely use it. Some
people like to have Teleportitis - it irritates me.
Warning.
Increased HIT and DAM.
Protection. Protection from Shape Changers, for completists only. 
You want both levitation and conflict extrinsically (in fact, I don't
think you _can_ have levitation as an intrinsic, except by
self-polymorph). 
You _don't_ want intrinsic regeneration - it burns food even while
you're not using it. 
Slow digestion, but you can't eat that ring regardless of material.

> Of course, the followup question is: having gained as many desirable  
> permanent properties as possible intrinsically, how do you fill the gaps  
> with extrinsics, given that there will inevitably be tradeoffs (e.g. boots  
> of speed vs jumping)?

I would suggest that the best thing to do, especially if you have never
ascended yet, is to stop worrying about getting the complete set, and
instead start work on getting further into the game. You are focusing on
something which is really a minor matter. 
You _should_ get the major resistances, but you will almost certainly
get those by eating corpses. The same thing is true for See Invisible,
although if you don't want invisibility yourself, you're more likely to
get that from the potion. Telepathy, which you get from a corpse (the
usual case) or amulet, not a ring. You want MR, MC2+, and reflection,
all extrinsically. Normally, you want extra speed rather than jumping -
the latter consumes food. And as I said above, levitation and conflict
extrinsically. SD is nice, not necessary.
Those are the only ones you should really care about. The rest are
inessential to ascension. I don't think I've ever ascended a character
who had eaten a ring or an amulet. Fretting about it may stop you from
paying attention to what is really important.
In that light, too, what character you start with should not depend on
what intrinsics you have, but how likely you are to survive the early
game and go on into the later stages. Because of that, until you ascend,
the best character to pick is a dwarvish valkyrie, dual-wielding
Excalibur, Frosty or Mjollnir with a katana.

